          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Mechanical engineering students get the best return from job oriented courses when they pick one area, such as design and CAD, manufacturing, quality and metrology, automation or thermal systems, and prove it with a finished part drawing or analysis that an engineer reviews."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "What sets mechanical apart: The work is judged by drawings, tolerances and parts that fit, so a clean part drawing is often a stronger proof than a certificate."
          }
        ]
